Description: lightweight Qt interface for the ClamAV antivirus
 Linux Defender is a native Qt 6 (QtWidgets) front-end for the ClamAV daemon
 (clamd), designed for KDE Plasma and its Breeze theme.
 .
 Features:
  - dashboard showing the protection status;
  - quick, full and custom scans, with progress, filters and exclusions;
  - automatic scan of USB keys and memory cards when they are mounted;
  - scan history;
  - quarantine: detected files moved away and made inert, restorable;
  - real-time protection (clamonacc), enabled at installation, with an
    on/off switch;
  - diagnostics of the installation (clamd service and socket, signatures,
    SELinux, scan limits), with one-click fixes (pkexec and polkit);
  - system tray icon showing the clamd status, with desktop notifications.
 .
 Files are opened by the application and passed to clamd (FILDES), so clamd
 can scan the home directory and removable media without reading them itself.
 clamd itself is only recommended: the socket path is configurable.
